      "side": 1,
      "message": "Going through the diffs offline, everything was falling into three categories:\n1. It was a large blur being rescaled and then hitting the simd algorithm, but being compared against a GPU implementation instead of a CPU image.\n2. It was a very small blur that used to be dropped as \"identity\" that was now being handled with the shader-based blur, so we were going from incorrectly having no blur to having some blur.\n3. It was a small blur that wasn\u0027t the identity, but was below the ~2 sigma value that is where the box blur approach\u0027s approximations break down, so we were switching from the simd algorithm to the more accurate shader algorithm.",
